  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Small and Medium Enterprise Assistance for Recovery and Transition (SMART)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(West Bank and Gaza):  . ..Despite modest recovery in the past year, the Palestinian economy continues to feel the aftereffects of the COVID-19 pandemic recession, sharply decreased donor support, and growing Israeli constraints on customs revenue transfers, as well as long-standing structural issues and growing arrears. This activity aims to mitigate these economic shocks as well as systemic constraints, and ultimately, jumpstart the competitiveness of firms with potential to increase market share and employment opportunities. SMART will help the Palestinian private sector regain productivity and build a future of sustainable growth in the West Bank, East Jerusalem, and Gaza (WBG)..Using FY22 Funds, this activity will continue to deliver rapid Recovery Assistance to firms amid the economic crisis. However, in order to truly achieve USAID&apos;s Objective to strengthen a sustainable Palestinian economy that creates jobs, stimulates growth, and attracts investment, SMART interventions will progress beyond recovery to prioritize firm-level growth and an improved business enabling environment (BEE). As the Recovery Plans initiated in FY22 conclude, SMART&apos;s two latest Programs, Private Sector Revitalization Program (REV), launched in June 2022, and the Institutional Capacity Building and Policy Program (a.k.a. SMART-BEE), launched in September 2022, will gain momentum over the course of 2023. REV will follow Recovery Plans with Revitalization Plans to invest in growth-oriented firms. SMART-BEE will partner with private sector organizations to address systemic constraints to growth at the institutional and policy level. Both programs already accumulated a growing pipeline of interested firms and institutional partners that will yield catalytic impact in FY 23 and beyond..This activity will contribute to the Microenterprise and Clean Energy earmarks..</narrative>
  </description>
